== Demographics ==
{{main|Demographics of Balisca}}
The Levante's population of 133,669,422 (determined in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]] using the broadest definition) makes it the most populous region of the Baliscan Confederation, containing approximately 62% of Balisca's total population. The population is concentrated in the central coastal corridor: the [[Concordia|Concordia conurbation]] alone accounts for approximately 25% of the Levante's total population, and the broader [[Silicon Coast]] urbanized zone contains over 40%. The northern and southern extremities are significantly less densely populated, though they have experienced growth in recent decades due to tourism, renewable energy development, and the decentralization policies of the [[Confederal government of Balisca|confederal government]].

The Levante is the most ethnically and linguistically diverse region of the confederation. The region's history as a zone of refuge, commercial exchange, and resistance produced a population that includes Kaftian-descended communities (particularly in [[Araucaria]] and the southern Levante), [[Cathar]]-descended communities (concentrated in [[Cerdanya]]), [[Mozbayani]] communities (in the historic Hesperian League ports), [[Sefardi]] communities (with a continuous presence since the colonial period), and indigenous peoples (particularly in the mountain zones and the southern interior). The [[Maroons|Maroon]] communities of Araucaria maintain distinctive cultural and linguistic traditions, including the [[Maroniko language]], which is one of the Balisca's recognized territorialized languages.

The Levante's demographic dynamism is sustained by [[Immigration to Balisca|continued immigration]], both from other regions of Balisca (particularly the [[Marañón basin]] of [[Bayara]] and [[Pindorama]]) and from abroad. The region's economic opportunities—particularly in the Silicon Coast's technology sector and the Blue-Tech marine industries—have made it the primary destination for both internal and international migrants. The 2025 census recorded that 24.1% of the Levante's population was foreign-born, slightly above the confederal average of 22.8%.

